{"agent":"Monster3-PS-snapshot-calibrate-7267fe","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"When the eviction loop attempts to delete an `others` file that has already been unlinked by a concurrent process, `f.unlink()` raises `FileNotFoundError`; `contextlib.suppress` catches it, but `total -= size` is inside the same `with` block and is skipped. The loop then continues with a total that still counts a file no longer on disk, so it evicts more snapshots than `max_bytes` requires. For example, with `max_bytes=1000` and three other snapshot files of 500 bytes each, if process A evicts the oldest file, process B’s first unlink fails, and B then evicts the second file too, leaving only the newest file even though the remaining two would have fit under the cap.","digest":"daede3c6d27093fc","location":"ddflow/infra/log/_read.py:_collect_stale_snapshots","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/infra/log/_read.py:_collect_stale_snapshots"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":18206,"diff_sha":"10d7ab91295f68903c7d34533d95d3d1444e8e5cff3eaeef6c93dc2559a76244","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":704.5,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"c88e5f12d511a482","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/PS-snapshot-calibrate.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261104T183504Z-0e06168d.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_for_holder":"[REDACTED:hostname]-PS-snapshot-calibrate-7267fe reviewed ps-snapcal's PS-snapshot-calibrate","reviewed_head":"3a3b2e1de70dd850537bdc136559bef6735b4643","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/config_sections/log.py":"100644 ac6cc111ecc6624e1c5287cdbd6567b23d91d6fc","ddflow/infra/log/_parse.py":"100644 fa43eaef4264b27983e58ffc385d292157